## Story Description
Implement the read endpoints that all dashboard pages consume. All data comes from direct Postgres queries against the views defined in US-002 or aggregations on the transactions table. No Parquet files. All endpoints are scoped to engagement_id and support standard filter query parameters. The diagnostics endpoint runs the existing DataQualityDiagnostics class from src/cube/diagnostics.py.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: backend/app/routers/cube.py — APIRouter with prefix='/api/engagements/{engagement_id}/cube', tags=['cube']
- All endpoints verify engagement ownership via verify_engagement_ownership() from backend/app/dependencies.py
- GET /overview — returns JSON: {total_spend: float, invoice_count: int, supplier_count: int, category_count: int, currency_label: str, maverick_spend_pct: float, tail_spend_pct: float, data_freshness: str (max invoice_date)}. All values computed via SQLAlchemy SELECT on transactions table WHERE engagement_id=? AND COALESCE(is_intercompany,0)=0 AND COALESCE(is_tax_line,0)=0. maverick_spend_pct = SUM(base_amount) WHERE po_number IS NULL / total_spend.
- GET /by-supplier — query params: limit=50, offset=0, sort_by=total_spend, order=desc, category_l1=, bu=, date_from=, date_to=, supplier_search= — SELECT from v_by_supplier WHERE engagement_id=? with applied filters; returns {data: list[SupplierRow], total_count: int}
- GET /by-category — query params: l1=, date_from=, date_to= — SELECT from v_by_category WHERE engagement_id=? with optional l1 filter; returns flat list sorted by total_spend DESC
- GET /by-month — SELECT from v_by_month WHERE engagement_id=? ORDER BY month ASC; computes rolling_3m_avg as 3-period rolling mean in Python (pandas rolling(3).mean()); returns list [{month: 'YYYY-MM', total_spend, transaction_count, rolling_3m_avg}]
- GET /by-payment-terms — SELECT from v_by_payment_terms WHERE engagement_id=?; computes spend_pct per bucket; computes wc_opportunity_aud using config.recommendations.target_payment_days and config.recommendations.wacc; returns list [{bucket, transaction_count, total_spend, spend_pct, wc_opportunity_aud}]
- GET /by-bu — SELECT from v_by_bu WHERE engagement_id=?; returns list [{business_unit, cost_centre, total_spend, transaction_count}]
- GET /diagnostics — imports src.cube.diagnostics.DataQualityDiagnostics; instantiates with engine and engagement_id; calls .run(); returns DiagnosticsReport as JSON dict including all 9 check results with status GREEN/AMBER/RED, value_pct, and description
- All query endpoints support date_from / date_to filtering as WHERE invoice_date >= date_from AND invoice_date <= date_to
- Register cube router in backend/app/main.py
- Verify: pytest backend/tests/test_cube_api.py -v — create this test file with at least: overview returns expected keys, by-month returns sorted list, by-supplier respects limit param

