Build the shared component library used across all five dashboard pages. These primitives — the filter sidebar, KPI metric tiles, and Recharts wrapper components — must be built correctly before the dashboard pages, as every page depends on them. Getting the design system consistent here means each dashboard page story can focus on layout and data.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: frontend/src/lib/formatters.ts — formatCurrency(value: number, currency='AUD'): string (e.g. '$1,234,567' or 'AUD 1,234,567'); formatPct(value: number): string (e.g. '12.3%'); formatNumber(value: number): string (comma-separated integer); formatDate(isoStr: string): string (DD MMM YYYY); formatMonth(isoStr: string): string (MMM YYYY)
- Create file: frontend/src/types/filters.ts — FilterState {date_from?: string, date_to?: string, business_units: string[], category_l1s: string[], supplier_search: string}; FilterOptions {business_units: string[], category_l1s: string[]}; defaultFilters(): FilterState returning empty state
- Create file: frontend/src/hooks/useFilters.ts — exports useFilters(): {filters: FilterState, updateFilter: (key, value) => void, clearFilters: () => void, toQueryParams: () => Record<string,string>}. Uses React useState. toQueryParams() omits empty/undefined values.
- Create file: frontend/src/components/dashboard/KpiCard.tsx — shadcn Card with: large bold value text (formatCurrency or formatNumber or formatPct depending on valueType prop), label in muted text below, optional delta row showing trend arrow icon (TrendingUp/TrendingDown from lucide-react) in green/red, optional subtext in xs muted. Props: {label, value: string|number, valueType?: 'currency'|'number'|'pct'|'text', delta?: number, deltaLabel?: string, currency?: string}
- Create file: frontend/src/components/dashboard/FilterBar.tsx — horizontal bar component. Props: {filters: FilterState, onChange: (f:FilterState)=>void, options: FilterOptions}. Renders: date-from input (type=date), date-to input, business-unit multi-select (shadcn Select with multiple prop or custom multi-select), category-l1 multi-select, supplier text search. 'Clear' button calls onChange(defaultFilters()). Only renders non-empty option arrays.
- Create file: frontend/src/components/charts/constants.ts — export CHART_COLORS = ['#1B4F72','#2E86C1','#5DADE2','#85C1E9','#AED6F1','#D6EAF8'] (SpendCube brand palette)
- Create file: frontend/src/components/charts/SpendBarChart.tsx — wraps Recharts: props {data: {label:string, value:number}[], title:string, horizontal?:boolean, color?:string, valueFormatter?:(v:number)=>string, maxItems?:number}. When horizontal=true renders BarChart with layout='vertical', YAxis type='category', XAxis type='number'. Includes ResponsiveContainer height=300, Tooltip with valueFormatter, no Legend.
- Create file: frontend/src/components/charts/SpendAreaChart.tsx — wraps Recharts AreaChart: props {data: MonthRow[], title:string, currency?:string}. Renders two Areas if rolling_3m_avg present (solid primary + dashed secondary). XAxis uses formatMonth formatter. Tooltip shows both series formatted as currency.
- Create file: frontend/src/components/charts/SpendPieChart.tsx — wraps Recharts PieChart + Pie: props {data: {name:string, value:number}[], title:string, valueFormatter?:(v:number)=>string}. Uses CHART_COLORS. Renders Legend below. Tooltip shows value formatted.
- Create file: frontend/src/components/charts/index.ts — re-exports all chart components
