- Edit file: frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx — wrap the 'Review Workstation' nav link in a conditional: only render if engagement?.is_admin === true. The engagement data should be fetched with useQuery(['engagement', id], () => api.get('/api/engagements/'+id).then(r=>r.data)) and stored in Layout context.
- Create file: frontend/src/pages/admin/ReviewWorkstationPage.tsx — add route guard: if !engagement?.is_admin return <Navigate to='../overview' replace/>.
- ReviewWorkstationPage renders shadcn Tabs with 4 tabs: 'Supplier Queue', 'Category Queue', 'Override Rules', 'Audit Log'.
- Supplier Queue tab: useQuery for GET /review/supplier-queue. shadcn Table: columns Raw Supplier, Matched To, Method, Confidence (badge colored by value: >=0.88 green, >=0.70 amber, else red). Action buttons per row: Approve (calls POST .../approve via useMutation, invalidates queue), Reject (calls POST .../reject), Override (opens shadcn Dialog with two inputs: New Canonical ID and New Name, confirm calls POST .../override). Show '0 items pending' empty state.
- Category Queue tab: useQuery for GET /review/category-queue. shadcn Table: columns Supplier, Amount (formatCurrency), Current L1/L2/L3, Confidence (badge). 'Override' button per row opens Dialog with: L1 Select (options from distinct category_l1 values in transactions), L2 Select (filtered to selected L1, populated client-side), L3 Select (filtered to selected L2), Reason textarea. Submit calls POST /review/category-override.
